{"name":"Dark Side","hex":"#004444","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark side","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of darkside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark_side"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Force","blocks":[{"text":"The Force is a metaphysical, mysterious, and ubiquitous power in the Star Wars fiction franchise. Within the galaxy in which the franchise is set, characters refer to the Force as an energy that interconnects all things, maintaining cosmic balance. Particularly \"Force-sensitive\" characters, usually through rigorous self-discipline, training, and mindfulness, are able to connect to the Force and thus access and wield certain supernatural abilities such as limited degrees of superhuman strength, telekinesis, and clairvoyance."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Force"},{"title":"Dark Side (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Side is a 1988 video game published by Incentive Software for the Amiga, Atari ST, Amstrad CPC, Commodore 64, IBM PC compatibles, ZX Spectrum, and Sharp MZ-800. The game is a sequel to Driller, set in the Evath system but this time on Evath's second moon Tricuspid."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Dark-side-inlay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Side_(video_game)"},{"title":"Dark Side (Kelly Clarkson song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Dark Side\" is a song by American singer Kelly Clarkson, written by Busbee and Alexander Geringas, and produced by Greg Kurstin. The song was released by RCA Records on June 5, 2012 as the third and final single from Clarkson's fifth studio album, Stronger (2011). \"Dark Side\" is a mid-tempo synth-pop ballad that incorporates a vigorous music box melody with up-tempo beats in choruses, with its lyrics containing the theme of acceptance, recovery, and inner-beauty."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Dark_Side_Single_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Side_(Kelly_Clarkson_song)"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/George_Lucas_cropped_2009.jpg/500px-George_Lucas_cropped_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/George_Lucas_cropped_2009.jpg/500px-George_Lucas_cropped_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"George Lucas created the concept of \"the Force\" both to advance the plot of Star Wars (1977) and to try to awaken a sense of spirituality in young audience members.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeorge_Lucas_cropped_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9b/Force_unleashed_concept.jpg/330px-Force_unleashed_concept.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9b/Force_unleashed_concept.jpg/330px-Force_unleashed_concept.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This concept art by Greg Knight of a stormtrooper being \"Force pushed\" was an early visualization of how the Force would be depicted in LucasArts' The Force Unleashed (2008).[30]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForce_unleashed_concept.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a0/Jedi_spirits-Return_of_the_Jedi_%281983%29.jpg/